And imaginary tables aren't tables (or anything else)(pace xorxes)  But 
generally, getting away from the principle that a broda brode is a brode makes 
more trouble than it is worth (I take it that the expression for hippopotamus -- 
if Lojban actually uses it [when would it?] -- is a compound that has just not 
been reduced and compounds can go anywhere.  It is important to notice, however, 
that broda brodes need not be broda (one of the nice things about Loglan that 
got lost was to make this explicit for an array of adjectives).  






